{
  "mn143:0.1": "Middle Discourses 143 ",
  "mn143:0.2": "Advice to Anāthapiṇḍika ",
  "mn143:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn143:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn143:2.1": "Now at that time the householder Anāthapiṇḍika was sick, suffering, gravely ill. ",
  "mn143:2.2": "Then he addressed a man, ",
  "mn143:2.3": "“Please, my man, go to the Buddha, and in my name bow with your head to his feet. Say to him: ",
  "mn143:2.4": "‘Sir, the householder Anāthapiṇḍika is sick, suffering, gravely ill. ",
  "mn143:2.5": "He bows with his head to your feet.’ ",
  "mn143:2.6": "Then go to Venerable Sāriputta, and in my name bow with your head to his feet. Say to him: ",
  "mn143:2.7": "‘Sir, the householder Anāthapiṇḍika is sick, suffering, gravely ill. ",
  "mn143:2.8": "He bows with his head to your feet.’ ",
  "mn143:2.9": "And then say: ",
  "mn143:2.10": "‘Sir, please visit him at his home out of sympathy.’” ",
  "mn143:2.11": "“Yes, sir,” that man replied. He did as Anāthapiṇḍika asked. ",
  "mn143:2.12": "",
  "mn143:2.13": "",
  "mn143:2.14": "",
  "mn143:2.15": "",
  "mn143:2.16": "",
  "mn143:2.17": "",
  "mn143:2.18": "",
  "mn143:2.19": "Sāriputta consented with silence. ",
  "mn143:3.1": "Then Venerable Sāriputta robed up and, taking his bowl and robe, went with Venerable Ānanda as his second monk to Anāthapiṇḍika’s home. He sat down on the seat spread out and said to